# Generated per-worktree agent hook, written by OhMyPiAdapter::prepare on every
# omp launch and carrying that machine's sirioctl path and that launch's pane id
# (#203). Its five siblings above are ignored for the same reason.
.sirio/
.idea/
skills-lock.json
.DS_Store
opencode.json
/.air/
/.codex/

# Python bytecode from the Linux verification scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local tool/IDE/planning artifacts — not shared repo content. docs/ stays
# local except two directories the repo itself depends on. Both need the
# `/docs/*` + `!` shape, because a parent excluded with `/docs/` could not
# be re-included:
#   - release-notes: release.yml refuses a tag whose
#     docs/release-notes/<version>.md is missing.
#   - superpowers/specs: shipped rustdoc links into them by URL (sirio_apply
#     alone carries nine), so an untracked spec is a 404 in published
#     documentation — and the auto-update spec those nine cite was lost
#     exactly this way. Implementation *plans* stay local on purpose: they
#     are execution scaffolding and go stale the moment the work lands.
/.codegraph/
/docs/*
!/docs/release-notes/
!/docs/superpowers/
/docs/superpowers/*
!/docs/superpowers/specs/
/output/
/plans/
